#=======================================================================
#  GRADE: Generalization Robustness Assessment for Detectors in Education
#
#  Rule of thumb (same as the LOGO repo): commit the CODE and the SMALL
#  DERIVED RESULTS the paper cites. Never commit corpora or model weights
#  — both are regenerable, and two of the corpora exceed GitHub's 100 MB
#  hard limit.
#=======================================================================

#---------------------------------------------------------------- models
# Fine-tuned checkpoints: ~500 MB each, 15 runs. Regenerate by running
# section 9 of notebooks/GRADE_full_study.ipynb.
models/
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth

#------------------------------------------------------------------ data
# Source corpora. Download instructions are in datasets/README.md:
#   llm_detect/  -> Kaggle "LLM - Detect AI Generated Text"
#   hf_pile/     -> huggingface.co/datasets/artem9k/ai-text-detection-pile
#   abstract_paraphrase/ -> github.com/kartelj/llm_plagiarism_public
# hf_pile_sample_20k.csv is 118 MB — over GitHub's limit.
datasets/**/*.csv
datasets/**/*.txt
!datasets/README.md

# Everything in data/ is built by section 1-8 of the notebook.
data/

# The rejected corpus retained as evidence for the audit claim (7 MB).
audit_evidence/

#--------------------------------------------------------------- results
# Per-run metrics and per-sample predictions ARE committed — they are what
# the paper cites and they are small. Figures are committed too.
# (nothing excluded here on purpose)

#----------------------------------------------------------------- latex
paper/*.aux
paper/*.log
paper/*.out
paper/*.toc
paper/*.synctex.gz
paper/*.fdb_latexmk
paper/*.fls
paper/*.bbl
paper/*.blg

#------------------------------------------------------------------ misc
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local tool settings
.claude/

# Prior work, kept locally as a code reference; it is its own repository.
Previous Logo Work/

# Third-party reference PDFs kept locally; not ours to redistribute.
*.pdf
!paper/iciser2026_short.pdf
